Mission:
Sustain forward combat power by delivering fuel, ammunition, and medical supplies from rear-area depots to the supported units across the operation window while minimizing total operational cost.

Execution/Concept:
- Source availability: Each depot’s outbound throughput by supply type and day is limited by on-hand stocks. Outflow must not exceed {DEPOT_SUPPLIES}. Preference should be given to secure, proximate depots to reduce exposure and {TRANSPORT_COSTS}.
- Demand satisfaction: Each unit’s daily requirement {DEMANDS} will be met by inbound flow. Controlled shortfalls are permitted as Slack and incur penalties {PENALTY_COSTS}. Slack is employed only when route risk or capacity constraints preclude timely delivery.
- Transport and capacity: Convoy loading adheres to vehicle capacity {VEHICLE_CAPACITY}, applying supply-specific volume factors {SUPPLY_VOLUMES}. Each vehicle deployed adds a cost {VEHICLE_COST} in addition to route-dependent transport costs {TRANSPORT_COSTS}.
- Routes and risk: Movement along any depot-to-unit corridor on a given day requires activating that route. Activating a route incurs a fixed security risk cost {RISK_COSTS}—covering escorts, route clearance, ISR overwatch, and QRF—regardless of the number of vehicles assigned. Vehicles may only operate on routes that are activated.
- Fleet management: The total number of vehicles employed across all routes each day cannot exceed the available fleet {TOTAL_VEHICLES}. Maintenance, crew rest, and staging constraints further limit convoy windows.
- Prioritization and phasing: Phase deliveries to maintain weapons readiness and maneuver, prioritizing ammunition prior to planned engagements, fuel to enable mobility, and protected movement for medical supplies. Where multiple corridors are available, balance lower transport costs against security risk and fixed activation overheads.
- Objective function: Select flows, route activations, and vehicle allocations to minimize the sum of transport costs {TRANSPORT_COSTS}, shortage penalties {PENALTY_COSTS}, per-vehicle deployment costs {VEHICLE_COST}, and fixed route security risk costs {RISK_COSTS}, while honoring depot capacity, demand, vehicle capacity, route activation, and fleet size constraints.

